WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.300
Text is normalized, tokenized, and wrapped
with special tokens. The result is a
sequence of token IDs—the first step
toward vectors.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:16.000
Attention masks mark real tokens with one
and padding with zero, so padding cannot
distort the later pooling step.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:25.150
The model returns token vectors. Mean
pooling combines only active positions
into one 384-dimensional vector
representing the input.

4
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:35.417
L2 normalization makes vector length
consistent. Cosine similarity then
compares direction, using the dot product
and norms while rejecting invalid values.

